    <DataNode elementId="AT1G05530-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-glycosyltransferase 75B2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZVY5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana UGT75B2&lt;/i&gt; gene was shown to encode a protein with glucosyltransferase activity |CITS:[LIM05]|. The enzyme was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; as a GST-fusion protein. The purified protein was assayed for its substrate specificity: the enzyme was shown to catalyze the glucosylation of the naturally-occuring |FRAME:CPD-693|, as well as its &apos;unnatural&apos; counterpart (-)-ABA |CITS:[LIM05]|.</Comment>
